WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.525
The execution plan has seven phases, and
each gate is the next phase's precondition.

2
00:00:05.525 --> 00:00:10.250
It runs from aligning the program,
through settling who owns each attribute,

3
00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:13.100
building and testing the
pipeline, and a pilot,

4
00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:17.150
to automating the lifecycle, cutting
over, and then sustaining it.

5
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.612
Four rules run through it.

6
00:00:18.612 --> 00:00:21.762
Start now, with the HR data
the agency already has,

7
00:00:21.762 --> 00:00:25.463
and switch the source to the
new platform when it arrives.

8
00:00:25.463 --> 00:00:30.412
Run in shadow mode first, comparing what
HR says with what the directories hold.

9
00:00:30.412 --> 00:00:35.801
Cut over one population at a time, with a
signed validation report and a rollback.

10
00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:40.500
And close the ticket path only when
the data proves HR is the sole source.

11
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.181
The gate thresholds, like
ninety-nine percent correlation,

12
00:00:44.181 --> 00:00:48.312
are proposals for the agency to
approve, not federal requirements.

13
00:00:48.312 --> 00:00:52.920
Chapter 13 walks an illustrative
agency through all seven phases.
